// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-032
=adr: 032
=title: Hierarchical Deletion Guards — Application, Device, Workflow
=date: 2026-02-26
=status: accepted_partial (Level1 implemented; Levels2-3 backlog)

#ctx
~problem: uneven deletion protection; Device had no guard → DeviceState/AlarmRule/AlarmInstance orphaned silently

=hierarchy: Organization → Application → [Device, Workflow, Dashboard]
  Device → [DeviceState, DeviceDerivedState, AlarmRule, AlarmInstance]
  Workflow → [WorkflowExecution (TTL 90d)]
!no_fk_constraints: MongoDB → guards enforced in service layer (ADR-001)

#decision
=level1_application: {
  block_409_if: Device.count({applicationId})>0 OR Workflow.count>0 OR Dashboard.count>0,
  response: blocking:{devices,workflows,dashboards}
}
=level2_device: {
  block_409_if: AlarmRule.count({deviceId,isActive:true})>0 OR AlarmInstance.count({deviceId,state:{$in:ACTIVE}})>0,
  auto_cascade: delete DeviceState(metadata.deviceId) + DeviceDerivedState(deviceId),
  response: blocking:{alarmRules,alarmInstances}
}
=level3_workflow: {
  no_block: WorkflowExecution retained as immutable history (TTL auto-expires 90d)
}

=impl_pattern: Promise.all for parallel counts → structured err.blocking → controller catches → 409
~frontend: parses blocking payload → renders entity count list in delete modal

#consequences
+pos: [ISA-18.2_compliant_device_delete, DeviceState_auto_purged, audit_history_preserved]
-neg: [operator_must_manually_clean_app_children_before_delete]

#scope
=arch_summary_update: yes
